<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Évreux</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mediolanum Aulercorum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Évreux is a city in Normandy, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eure">Eure</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. It began as Mediolanum Aulercorum, the Roman capital of the Gallic Eburovices, from whom its name derives. A bishopric from late antiquity and the seat of a medieval county, it has a cathedral built over several centuries in Romanesque and Gothic styles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/evreux.jpg" alt="Évreux" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miwok from France · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_d%27%C3%89vreux_(17512240920).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
